# Shell scripts must be LF whatever the checkout platform.
#
# Earned the hard way: `install.sh` was authored on Windows with `core.autocrlf`
# on, so the checkout had CRLF, and every line ended in a `\r` the shell treated
# as part of the command. On the server that produced
#
#   scripts/install.sh: 22: : not found
#   scripts/install.sh: 23: set: Illegal option -
#
# which names neither the file's real problem nor the line that has it. An
# installer is the one file guaranteed to run on a machine that is not the one it
# was written on, so this is not a preference.
*.sh text eol=lf
